{"title":"What should I ask Annie Lowrey?","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/968111837/0/marginalrevolution~What-should-I-ask-Annie-Lowrey.html","date":1787380668000,"content":"<p>Yes I will be doing a Conversation with her.  She has a new and very interesting book coming out, namely <span><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Time-Tax-Government-Wastes-Time_and/dp/0063442558/ref=sr_1_1?crid=26IUEBFINPWAD&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.uGgyyxuWDYCnWag8zsxby03x3dahrvRSsvd5tqmrOqNxcDGa2hQy8noqXU7_PgvaMU8wbSBzC-UwwbL_9QfEjw.hxtZSoVcZu6kWBSguc1PKR6R0e26GJXBGcriar141qE&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=annie%2Blowrey&amp;qid=1787333783&amp;sprefix=annie%2Blowrey%2Caps%2C159&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">The Time Tax: How the Government Wastes Our Time―and How to Fix It</a>.  More generally, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Annie_Lowrey\" target=\"_blank\">from Wikipedia</a>:</span></p>\r\n<blockquote><p><b>Annie M. Lowrey…</b>is an American journalist who writes on politics and economic policy for <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Atlantic\">The Atlantic</a></i>.<sup></sup> Previously, Lowrey covered economic policy for <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times\">The New York Times</a></i> and prior to that was the Moneybox columnist for <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slate_(magazine)\">Slate</a>.</i><sup></sup> She was also a <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Staff_writer\">staff writer</a> for the <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_Independent\">Washington Independent</a></i> and was on the editorial staffs of <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_Policy\">Foreign Policy</a></i> and <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_Yorker\">The New Yorker</a></i>.<sup></sup> She is a proponent of <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universal_basic_income\">universal basic income</a>.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>So what should I ask her?</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/08/what-should-i-ask-annie-lowrey.html\">What should I ask Annie Lowrey?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/968111837/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/968111837/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/968111837/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/968111837/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/968111837/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/20/968111837/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/rss20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/08/what-should-i-ask-annie-lowrey.html#comments\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/comments20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/08/what-s